/-!
# G.3: Some groups generated by transvections

The source statement is Lemma G.3.1, printed pp. 337--338 of the combined
1 March 2004 Aschbacher--Smith manuscript (PDF pp. 348--349). Its three
conclusions require full linear actions on the generated-group orbit spans,
internal direct decompositions, the local rank formula, and dimension at
least three. The shared source interface retains these exact obligations.

`source_conclusions_of_twoCore_eq_bot` proves all these conclusions with the
additional hypothesis that the actual faithful acting group has trivial
intrinsic two-core. Its recognition, decomposition and local-rank inputs are
all discharged. `dual_source_conclusions_of_twoCore_eq_bot` proves the dual
form, using the actual contragredient action, equality of action kernels,
transport of the intrinsic core, and the axis/center radical correspondence.
Both results retain the extra two-core hypothesis for consumers to discharge;
neither assumes irreducibility or semisimplicity.

The unrestricted printed lemma is not asserted. The checked fixed-vector
obstruction in `Recognition.FixedVectorObstruction` is preserved; the quotient
rank premise of that example is still only GAP-verified, so it is not a complete
Lean counterexample to the printed statement.
-/
